  "title": "Rocket Failure Wipes Out 40 Amazon Leo Satellites #shorts",
  "description": "On November 15, a United Launch Alliance Vulcan rocket carrying 40 Amazon Leo internet satellites suffered an anomaly about ten minutes after liftoff from Cape Canaveral and failed to reach orbit, ULA said. Spaceflight Now reports the problem came during the Centaur upper-stage burn; the cause is under investigation. It was the first of 38 Vulcan launches Amazon bought, and the Pentagon had been waiting on this flight before clearing Vulcan for national security launches again, according to Reuters.\n\nSources: ULA statement, Spaceflight Now, Space.com, Reuters (via IBTimes, Militarnyi), Engadget, Via Satellite, WESH.\n\n#tech #space #AmazonLeo #ULA #Vulcan",
